The Unix tools for bash: suckless sbase (git.suckless.org/sbase, master
2026-04-03, MIT) built with DJGPP, 80 programs in C:\BIN (C: only):

  ls cp mv rm mkdir rmdir touch ln link unlink chmod du find xargs
  cat head tail wc sort uniq cut paste join comm tr sed grep ed fold nl
  expand unexpand rev tee sponge split tsort cols strings od
  basename dirname readlink pathchk mktemp which env printenv
  date cal sleep time true false yes echo printf test expr seq bc dc
  tar uuencode uudecode cmp cksum md5sum sha1sum sha224sum sha256sum
  sha384sum sha512sum dd sync tty uname logname whoami

sbase is POSIX and small: the options POSIX has (ls -l, sort -n, grep -E,
sed -n, find -name -type -exec), not GNU's long ones (--color, sed -i).

PATH: AUTOEXEC.BAT puts C:\BIN last, so at the DOS prompt `ls' works and FIND,
SORT and DATE are still DOS's; bash puts C:/BIN first, so in bash they are the
Unix ones. (An AUTOEXEC.BAT from before this keeps its PATH when esp.img is
updated; bash adds C:\BIN by itself either way.)

  TOOLS            the tools built, one per line
  sbase-dos.patch  the changes to sbase:
                   ls      on the screen, names in columns (the BIOS's width),
                           as GNU's and BSD's ls do; -1 and -l, and pipes,
                           one per line
                   which   DOS's PATH (C:\BIN;C:\DOS) and .EXE/.COM/.BAT
                   bc      dc runs on bc's output when bc's input ends (DOS
                           runs one program at a time): echo 2^64 | bc
                   ls, cp, touch: file times without nanoseconds;
                   du: sizes from st_size (DJGPP has no st_blocks)
  dos/sbase-dos.h, sbase-dos.c
                   what DJGPP lacks: the *at() calls, directories opened as
                   file descriptors (DOS can't), utimensat (and file times
                   through INT 21h 5701h when DOSLFN's call fails),
                   fmemopen, strptime, getline, tsearch, and fork-and-exec
                   for find -exec, xargs, time and env (the program runs
                   at once with spawn; waitpid gets its status)
  LICENSE          sbase's (MIT)

Files are read and written as they are (binary); the screen and keyboard
stay text, so lines end where they should.

Left out: what DOS has no use for or can't do: chgrp, chown, chroot, cron,
flock, getconf, hostname, kill (bash has it), logger, mkfifo, mknod, nice,
nohup, renice, setsid, tftp, install; sha512-224sum and sha512-256sum (long
names); sbase's make. On DOS, ln copies (no links) and chmod only sets or
clears read-only.

Nothing prebuilt is kept: make builds deps/sbase/*.EXE with tools/build-sbase.sh
(DJGPP gcc 12, -O2 -march=i486, UPX --best) from sbase's git at a pinned commit
(git.suckless.org, or a mirror), with the DJGPP cross compiler from
tools/get-djgpp.sh (deps/djgpp) unless one is on PATH. CI keeps deps/ in its cache.
